<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Visoun</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. 1500–1520</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Visounarath</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Visoun was king of Lan Xang from 1500 to 1520. He brought the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/phra-bang">Phra Bang</a>, the revered Buddha image, to the capital, which was later renamed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/luang-prabang">Luang Prabang</a> after it, and founded Wat Visoun there. His reign saw the rebuilding of the kingdom after the Vietnamese invasion of 1479 and the writing of an early Lao chronicle.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/visoun.jpg" alt="Visoun" width="320" height="199" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Louis Delaporte (Life time: 1842-1925) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Wat_Visoun,_Luang_Prabang_Laos_by_Louis_Delaporte.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
